<PARA INFOID = "T060077A465" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Brake Actuator</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Consists of master cylinder cut solenoid valves, holding solenoid valves, pressure reduction solenoid valves, a pump, reservoirs, etc., and regulates the brake hydraulic pressure to each wheel cylinder. In addition, the brake actuator and skid control computer are integrated to reduce size.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "k4730036c" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.958in" />
</FIGURE>
<INDICATE ID = "T060077A465I01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Hydraulic Circuit Diagram</TITLE>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "k4250212c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "7.306in" />
</FIGURE>
</INDICATE>

<MECA ID = "T060077A465A240" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "2Oct2003"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Holding and Pressure Reduction Solenoid Valves</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Two solenoid valves are operated by control signals from the skid control computer to switch the brake hydraulic circuit among 3 modes: pressure increase, holding and pressure reduction.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T060077A465A186" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "16Sep2003"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Master Cylinder Cut Solenoid Valve</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Linear solenoid valves are used as the master cylinder cut solenoid valves, smoothing hydraulic pressure changes during brake assist control.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By controlling the open and closed state of the valves, the hydraulic pressure generated by the pump is regulated, making it possible to generate control hydraulic pressure according to the operating condition.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740191c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "3.167in" />
</FIGURE>
</MECA>

<MECA ID = "T060077A465A188" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "16Sep2003"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Master Cylinder Pressure Sensor</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The master cylinder pressure sensor is built into the brake actuator. Outputs the master cylinder pressure signal to the skid control computer.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "k4250214c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "2.181in" />
</FIGURE>
</MECA>

<MECA ID = "T060077A465A113" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "16Sep2003"     MECATYPE = "ACTUATE" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>ABS with EBD Operation</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Hydraulic pressure control of the 4 wheels is performed by operating the holding and pressure reduction solenoid valves, pump and reservoirs.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "k4250215c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "4.153in" />
</FIGURE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1"><TITLE>Control Operation</TITLE>
<TGROUP COLS = "4" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
